{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01WPRgG3m6kvco6Wu9oyWWbg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the grounded summary. Note one anchor caveat up front: of the two named member documents, **`foreman.config.json` is present and the Execution Log carries only its Crucible Stage-2 seed — Foreman appended no per-wave entries below the seed line**, so the outcome claims below are grounded in the sibling planning docs (DESCRIPTION/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN) and the observed shipped files, not in log entries.\n\n## runtime-host — build trio session summary\n\n**Scope & intent (from DESCRIPTION.md)**\n- Built the **missing Tier-1 deterministic runtime host** for the already-shipped Gandalf v1 skill — the \"thin runtime entry\" the prior build log flagged as an open follow-up.\n- Purpose: take a live analysis's **RAW draft** (un-stamped findings/elevations/diagnosis) and run it through the **already-shipped seam engine** (`seam/*.mjs`) to emit a **canary-conformant, honestly-graded** advisor output — making grades *deterministic* instead of model-self-asserted.\n- Explicitly **Tier-1 only**: runs the deterministic seam pass on ONE model run; does **not** dispatch live independent refuters or the researchPrime SITUATE commission (those need the `agent()` seam, flagged the integration point the gate never runs). That live-refuter PROMISING tier is a **sequenced follow-on, out of scope**.\n\n**Honesty / grading invariants (DESCRIPTION.md)**\n- Every **elevation** honestly lands at **SPECULATIVE** carrying `NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP` (the seam's own honest floor, since no independent refutation ran).\n- **Diagnosis** findings keep their evidence rungs + `gandalf_core` provenance; **risk_labels** capped at single-family **PROMISING** (`cross_model:false`); only **REFUTED** items drop.\n- Non-negotiables: reuse shipped seams (never reimplement grading), never weaken the existing 130 canary tests, malformed draft → honest named error (no fabricated/forged output), additive-only changes.\n\n**Build config (foreman.config.json)**\n- Project `gandalf-runtime-host`; gate command `node --test test/*.test.mjs`; `git:false` (Foreman git hygiene off for this run); docs trio wired to DESCRIPTION / IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN / EXECUTION-LOG.\n\n**Pre-build state (Execution Log seed)**\n- Plan = 3 waves, terminal committed milestone = Wave 3. Baseline: Gandalf v1 shipped at **130/130** tests (re-verify at start).\n- Gate is deterministic; the live-refuter `agent()` dispatch is **out of scope and out of the gate**. HALT-worthy triggers: any change to shipped seams/schema/canary, or reaching for the `agent()` refuter seam.\n\n**Planned waves (IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md)**\n- **Wave 1** — `runtime/seam-pass.mjs` (`applySeamPass`): validate draft shape (throw `SeamPassInputError` on malformed), route findings by kind (diagnose/anticipate/situate), vet+downgrade elevations to SPECULATIVE-stamped, compose risk_labels, propagate `degraded` to top-level (B6).\n- **Wave 2** — `runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` CLI (`--input`/stdin → `--output`/stdout, non-zero exit + no partial output on failure) + `runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`.\n- **Wave 3** — integration test + docs (`SKILL.md §RUNTIME`, LESSONS, journal) flipping the host from \"aspirational\" to real.\n\n**Observed outcome (shipped files + git history)**\n- All three waves' deliverables exist: `runtime/seam-pass.mjs`, `runtime/gandalf-run.mjs`, `runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`, plus `test/runtime-seam-pass`, `runtime-entry`, `runtime-integration`, and an **extra `runtime-robustness.test.mjs`** + `runtime-fixtures.mjs` (coverage beyond the plan).\n- Landed in commit `cd24857` (\"land the Tier-1 deterministic runtime host (+ commit the shipped v1 bundle)\"), then **two post-landing hardening commits** capturing live-run lessons: `a1a48f6` \"lenient input / strict output (the live-smoke lesson)\" and `40584ca` \"sanitize out-of-enum values too (the 6-project-run lesson)\" — i.e. the host was exercised on real runs after landing and tightened.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the `report.md` currently in the working tree is an unrelated **researchPrime study on Foreman parallelism**, not an artifact of this runtime-host session — I excluded it from the summary. Want me to fold in the actual test count by running the gate, or is the doc-grounded summary sufficient?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370,"cache_read_input_tokens":40674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":370},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35ce36be-dd7e-428a-a4e4-c42a685d61d6","uuid":"7ca4a593-1e03-4ab1-a65c-f78b93aca27c","request_id":"req_011CcLjcfVfeppvWKpoWSkie"}
